WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.167 --> 00:00:02.834
(curious music)

00:00:05.859 --> 00:00:07.640
- If you have money that's
been damaged in a fire,

00:00:07.640 --> 00:00:10.970
in a flood, that's been
eaten by insects or animals,

00:00:10.970 --> 00:00:13.270
we'll evaluate and
determine how much is there

00:00:13.270 --> 00:00:15.441
and reimburse you for it.

00:00:15.441 --> 00:00:18.490
(curious music)

00:00:18.490 --> 00:00:20.400
My name is Eric Walsh,
I'm the assistant manager

00:00:20.400 --> 00:00:22.460
at the Mutilated Currency Division.

00:00:22.460 --> 00:00:24.760
Every year, the Mutilated
Currency Division

00:00:24.760 --> 00:00:27.460
receives about 23,000 cases,
people will send money

00:00:27.460 --> 00:00:28.750
that's been somehow damaged,

00:00:28.750 --> 00:00:31.670
and we reimburse, annually,
about 40 million dollars.

00:00:31.670 --> 00:00:33.050
It's a free service
the government provides

00:00:33.050 --> 00:00:34.700
that we pay dollar in dollar out.

00:00:36.200 --> 00:00:38.900
We require 51 percent of the
note present to pay on it

00:00:38.900 --> 00:00:39.733
and that just protects us

00:00:39.733 --> 00:00:41.980
from paying twice on the same note.

00:00:41.980 --> 00:00:43.190
Once we determine the amount,

00:00:43.190 --> 00:00:45.770
we will send a treasury
check for what we discover.

00:00:51.190 --> 00:00:52.280
We're pretty low-tech here,

00:00:52.280 --> 00:00:56.210
so the tools of the trade are
scissors, knives, scalpels,

00:00:56.210 --> 00:00:58.360
glue and tape, and maybe
a pair of tweezers.

00:00:59.310 --> 00:01:01.840
The most challenging cases
are usually cases that

00:01:01.840 --> 00:01:04.840
the money has gotten wet and
sat for long periods of times,

00:01:04.840 --> 00:01:07.820
and it'll actually petrify
and be solid as a brick.

00:01:07.820 --> 00:01:09.620
A lot of it is "the dog ate my money."

00:01:09.620 --> 00:01:11.800
We get hundreds of those cases a year.

00:01:12.793 --> 00:01:13.836
A lot of people

00:01:13.836 --> 00:01:15.470
will hide their money in the
oven and forget about it,

00:01:15.470 --> 00:01:17.250
or they'll get it wet and
put it in the microwave

00:01:17.250 --> 00:01:18.950
and that will ignite the currency.

00:01:20.740 --> 00:01:23.450
Our most infamous case
took place in the '80s,

00:01:23.450 --> 00:01:26.740
and what happened was a farmer
lost his wallet in a field

00:01:26.740 --> 00:01:28.580
and discovered that his cow had eaten it,

00:01:28.580 --> 00:01:30.810
and we always encourage the submitter

00:01:30.810 --> 00:01:33.060
to send in the package as it is;

00:01:33.060 --> 00:01:35.850
and the farmer sent in the cow's stomach,

00:01:35.850 --> 00:01:37.910
which we were able to
retrieve the wallet from

00:01:37.910 --> 00:01:40.210
and reimburse the farmer his currency.

00:01:45.070 --> 00:01:47.230
Our office consists of
just under 20 people,

00:01:47.230 --> 00:01:48.500
and we have 12 people

00:01:48.500 --> 00:01:51.390
that examine and process the submissions,

00:01:51.390 --> 00:01:52.490
and they do roughly between

00:01:52.490 --> 00:01:54.400
1,000 and 2,000 claims each year.

00:01:56.570 --> 00:01:58.570
We do get an increased amount of cases

00:01:58.570 --> 00:02:00.760
after a natural disaster.

00:02:00.760 --> 00:02:03.030
Over the past year between the hurricanes

00:02:03.030 --> 00:02:04.200
and wildfires out in California,

00:02:04.200 --> 00:02:06.400
we've reimbursed over two million dollars.

00:02:06.400 --> 00:02:08.350
We're called upon when a lot
of people hit their low point,

00:02:08.350 --> 00:02:10.314
so any relief that you
could provide someone

00:02:10.314 --> 00:02:12.450
after they lost all their money in a flood

00:02:12.450 --> 00:02:15.570
or after their house burned
down is very rewarding.

00:02:17.040 --> 00:02:19.260
Hopefully we're a service that
you will never need to use,

00:02:19.260 --> 00:02:21.910
but in case something does
happen, we're here for you.

00:02:27.089 --> 00:02:30.006
(electronic chime)

